WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.140
Have you ever finished a terrible movie
just because you paid for the ticket?

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.090
Congratulations.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.440
You've experienced the sunk cost fallacy.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.430
It's when we continue something simply
because we've already invested time,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.050
money or effort into it.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.300
Imagine buying an expensive online course.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.730
You realise after two
lessons that it's useless.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.230
But instead of stopping,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.890
you force yourself to finish
it because you've already paid.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:24.240
Here's the catch:
the money is already gone.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.110
Continuing won't bring it back.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.840
Sometimes the smartest decision
is knowing when to walk away.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.270
What's something you've continued only
because you had already invested too much

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:33.860
in it?

